        <!-- Closing -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Measure the floor area and pick the blade span from the chart, sizing up when in doubt. Measure the ceiling and pick a downrod that puts the blades 8 to 9 feet up, never below 7. Keep the tips 18 inches from the walls, and check CFM on the EnergyGuide label before you pay.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Get those numbers right and almost any decent fan will work. For the ones we would actually hang, by size and room type, see our <a href="/best-ceiling-fans-with-lights/" class="text-[#38BDF8]">tested ceiling fans with lights</a>.
          </p>
